data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc`'d `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>`.** The syntax is straightforward:

```csharp
Span<nint> span = stackalloc nint[5];
Span<nuint> uspan = stackalloc nuint[3];
```

It compiled and ran without issues on .NET 11. On this 64-bit machine, `nint` is 8 bytes and `nuint.MaxValue` is `18446744073709551615` (2⁶⁴−1). This has been supported since C# 9 / .NET 5 when `nint`/`nuint` were introduced as first-class unmanaged types (which is the requirement for `stackalloc`).
